## Report

Task 2 (ByteReader and ByteWriter) is complete. Here's what was implemented:

### Files Created

1. **`src/core/reader.ts`** - ByteReader implementation with:
   - All read methods: `u8`, `u16le`, `u16be`, `u32le`, `u32be`, `i8`, `i16le`, `i32le`, `f64le`, `bytes(n, label)`, `nullString(label, maxLen?)`, `skip(n, label)`, `seek(offset)`
   - `group(label, fn)` for creating nested annotation spans
   - `annotations()` method to return collected annotations
   - Read-only properties: `offset`, `size`, `remaining`
   - Every read automatically records an Annotation span with label, start/end offsets, and optional value

2. **`src/core/writer.ts`** - ByteWriter implementation with:
   - All write methods: `writeU8`, `writeU16le`, `writeU16be`, `writeU32le`, `writeU32be`, `writeI16le`, `writeI32le`, `writeF64le`, `writeBytes`
   - `toUint8Array()` to return the written bytes
   - Read-only property: `length`
   - Automatic buffer capacity growth

3. **`src/core/reader.test.ts`** - Example tests covering:
   - All read methods with expected values
   - Bounds checking behavior (throws ExhumeError)
   - Group nesting
   - Seek and skip functionality
   - Annotation coverage (no gaps, no overlaps)

4. **`src/core/writer.test.ts`** - Example tests covering:
   - All write methods with expected values
   - Round-trip with DataView reads

5. **`src/core/reader.prop.test.ts`** - Property tests (fast-check) covering:
   - **P3: Annotations are honest** - for fully-read files, annotations cover every byte exactly once with no gaps or overlaps

